[FINAL-TEXT] All the evidence is in. I have direct confirmation from every layer:

- `cs_lab1` gets **"Destination Net Unreachable"** sourced from `192.168.2.1` (router0's own gateway) for every non-local destination — server room, internet lab, and even the office.
- `router0`'s routing table contains **only its three directly-connected prefixes** — zero RIP-learned routes.
- `ripd is not running` (confirmed by `show ip rip`).
- `/etc/frr/daemons` on router0 has `ripd=no`.
